</section></score></mdiv></body>
<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>So also deeper into Thee</l><l>I’d make my home, my rest in Thee;</l><l>A pillar in Thy temple be</l><l>And stay in Thee eternally.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Thy precious blood was shed that we</l><l>Could closer, closer, closest be;</l><l>In resurrection brought to Thee</l><l>That we might be as one as Thee.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>My lovely Lord, my dear Bridegroom,</l><l>In trust I open ev’ry room;</l><l>This mind, emotion, will be Thine;</l><l>When Thou hast rest, that rest is mine.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>Oh mystery of mysteries—</l><l>Lord, Thou in me and I in Thee!</l><l>The church, Thy temple—we to Thee,</l><l>And Thee our tabernacle be.</l></lg>
<lg label="6."><l>Lord, make Thy home more ev’ry day,</l><l>’Til one with Thee in ev’ry way,</l><l>’Til on me write Thy holy name,</l><l>’Til on me write Thy city’s name.</l></lg>
<lg label="7."><l>Lord, Thou art me and I am Thee,</l><l>As lovers coinhering, we;</l><l>Soon then shall come eternity</l><l>When God and man dwell mutually.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
